menu "GBX UI"

config GBX_UI_STATIC_SHELL
    bool "Draw the shell once"
    default n
    help
        The game page draws the on-screen controls once, as they look
        unpressed, and does not show presses; only the speed switch follows
        its position. It shows no VFD readings either, so the board's layout
        has no VFD cells. The shared sdkconfig.defaults.<target> file of a
        chip with one core enables it, where each redraw takes time from
        the emulation.

config GBX_UI_PACK_IN_FLASH
    bool "Draw the VFD from the asset pack in flash"
    default n
    help
        The game page's VFD reads its font atlases and the shell under its
        cells where they lie in the asset pack, in flash, instead of copies
        in PSRAM. The copies take about 640 KB on an 800x480 layout; without
        them each redraw of a reading reads flash. A board whose PSRAM is
        short enables it in boards/<board>/sdkconfig.defaults.

endmenu
